    "body": "Problem:\r\nIf a job exits with cursor at last row, the `[Process exited]` message\r\ncovers the text of that row.\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\nStart a new line before showing the message, like the old\r\n`\\r\\n[Process exited]` did.\r\n\r\nfix https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/42334\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-14T11:27:55Z",
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "_links": {
                "html": {
                    "href": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42349#discussion_r4273037769"
                },
                "pull_request": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/42349"
                },
                "self": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/comments/4273037769"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Sorry if it's a dummy question, but I must be missing something.\r\nWhy is this line `if (term->textbuf[0] != NUL)` needed?\r\n\r\nConsider these two tests below, they can pass under the current implementation:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n  it('short output that ends with an empty line', function()\r\n    local screen = Screen.new(50, 7)\r\n    local chan = api.nvim_open_term(0, {})\r\n    api.nvim_chan_send(chan, ('meow\\r\\n'):rep(1) .. 'LAST LINE\\n')\r\n    fn.chanclose(chan)\r\n    feed('i')\r\n    screen:expect([[\r\n      meow                                              |\r\n      LAST LINE                                         |\r\n      ^                                                  |\r\n      [Terminal closed]                                 |\r\n                                                        |*2\r\n      {5:-- TERMINAL --}                                    |\r\n    ]])\r\n  end)\r\n```\r\n```lua\r\n  it('output that fills screen and ends with an empty line', function()\r\n    local screen = Screen.new(50, 7)\r\n    local chan = api.nvim_open_term(0, {})\r\n    api.nvim_chan_send(chan, ('meow\\r\\n'):rep(10) .. 'LAST LINE\\n')\r\n    fn.chanclose(chan)\r\n    feed('i')\r\n    screen:expect([[\r\n      meow                                              |*4\r\n      LAST LINE                                         |\r\n      ^[Terminal closed]                                 |\r\n      {5:-- TERMINAL --}                                    |\r\n    ]])\r\n  end)\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut they behave differently:\r\n- with `('meow\\r\\n'):rep(1) .. 'LAST LINE\\n'`, there is an empty line between `LAST LINE` and `[Terminal closed]`\r\n- with `('meow\\r\\n'):rep(10) .. 'LAST LINE\\n'`, there is no empty line between them.\r\n\r\nShould the second case have that empty line too?",
            "commit_id": "1b1956d4f10c751b396b633d3695b1a3e699dfa1",
            "created_at": "2026-10-14T15:48:01Z",
